🚽 Test case: round-16 review finding #2 -- the array-shape hazard was only
🚽 one instance of a broader problem with a variadic native's unchecked
🚽 tail: "unchecked type" was being treated as "unchecked representation
🚽 validity". A struct identifier has no VAR_STRUCT case in
🚽 ast_expr_to_stdrot_value()'s NODE_IDENTIFIER switch (stdrot.c), so it
🚽 would fall through leaving the marshalled StdrotValue at its
🚽 initialized STDROT_NONE -- yapping("%d", f) would silently hand its
🚽 formatter "no value" where the source plainly supplied a struct.
🚽 is_unmarshallable_expr() (semantic_analyzer.c) now rejects this
🚽 statically, the same way it already rejects an unmarshallable array.
gang Foo {
    rizz x;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Foo f = { 42 };
    yapping("%d", f);
    bussin 0;
}
